      "writtenOn": "2025-10-14T23:08:35Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Can the PNG decoders actually output in all these color types?",
      "revId": "124da8ded1088878a8fd041c442ae6bb1697acac",
      "serverId": "fca2d64a-0420-3532-b200-12848c95a47b"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "83cabadf_fdb89213",
        "filename": "core/fxcodec/png/skia_png_decoder.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 23
      },
      "lineNbr": 63,
      "author": {
        "id": 7232
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-10-14T23:35:17Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Encoded PNG pixels are actually a subset of these formats (various-bit-depths X (G, GA, RGB, RGBA, Indexed)).  But some PNG chunks (like [sBIT](https://www.w3.org/TR/png-3/#11sBIT)) can influence which color format Skia will recommend for decoder clients (e.g. see [here](https://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/src/+/main:third_party/skia/src/codec/SkPngRustCodec.cpp;l\u003d48-50;drc\u003d593c8eb07c6dcff050fdf70a8df1347417615bd4)).\n\nWe could in theory say `NOTREACHED` for color formats that are not used by Skia today.  But it seems more robust to handle all the enum values.\n\nBut... looking at this a bit more, it seems that `PngEncodedColorType src_color_type` is *only* used to calculate the number of components (in [`core/fxcodec/progressive_decoder.cpp`](https://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/src/+/main:third_party/pdfium/core/fxcodec/progressive_decoder.cpp;l\u003d99;drc\u003d1a1c55244b379198ca0eaa9498c1fd527850abb2)).  So I think I should refactor things (in a separate, prerequisite CL) to just pass the number of components instead of mapping color formats from one enum to another.\n\nLeaving this unresolved for now - I\u0027ll address it later (as part of rebasing on top of the other CL I am planning above).",
      "parentUuid": "7aa0c35a_6d49a914",
      "revId": "124da8ded1088878a8fd041c442ae6bb1697acac",
      "serverId": "fca2d64a-0420-3532-b200-12848c95a47b"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "a41a7d28_c9b2459a",
        "filename": "core/fxcodec/png/skia_png_decoder.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 23
      },
      "lineNbr": 63,
      "author": {
        "id": 7232
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-10-15T00:02:44Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Done.  Although we still need to handle all the different Skia color types here.  AFAICT there is no public Skia API to directly get the number of components in `SkImageInfo` and/or `SkColorType`.  I think this is okay.",
      "parentUuid": "83cabadf_fdb89213",
      "revId": "124da8ded1088878a8fd041c442ae6bb1697acac",
      "serverId": "fca2d64a-0420-3532-b200-12848c95a47b"
    },
